{#
  NTP client -- Cisco NX-OS.

  WHY THIS DEVICE HAS ONE: nxos runs under vrnetlab, so it is a QEMU VM with its OWN clock,
  not a container sharing the host's. Measured on a live n9kv before this template existed:
  host 21:00:00 UTC, VM 20:55:52 UTC -- 4m08s adrift. Worse, that VM already claimed
  "Time source is NTP" with no server configured anywhere, so the device's own status output
  asserts a synchronisation it has not earned. Do not use it to check this worked; use
  `show ntp peers` (lists the configured server) and `show ntp peer-status` (shows whether it
  is actually reachable and selected).

  VRF: mgmt0 lives in the `management` VRF on NX-OS, and it is the only interface with a path
  to the gateway, so the request has to be sourced there or it is never answered.
#}
{#
  ---- SHARED NOTE (kept in both ntp templates) --------------------------------------------
  THE SERVER ADDRESS IS DERIVED, NOT HARD-CODED. It is the lab's management gateway, which on
  any netlab host is the host itself -- the box where chronyd runs. Deriving it keeps this
  correct under any multilab id (the mgmt network is 192.168.<id>.0/24) and on any netlab
  host, instead of pinning one box's address into the fork.

  THE TWO RENDER CONTEXTS ARE NOT THE SAME, and this is the trap that cost the first attempt:
    * netlab renders this at `netlab create` time with its OWN Jinja environment, where the
      management pool is `addressing.mgmt.ipv4`; `pools` does NOT exist.
    * Ansible renders it again at `netlab initial` time, where the same data is `pools.mgmt`
      (outputs/ansible.py copies topology.addressing into `pools`); `addressing` does NOT
      exist.
  A template using only one of them fails in the other context. Using only `pools` failed at
  create time with a bare "'width' is undefined" -- netaddr choking on an Undefined value,
  an error that names nothing useful. Hence the explicit either/or below.
#}
{% set _mgmt_pool = addressing.mgmt.ipv4 if addressing is defined else pools.mgmt.ipv4 %}
ntp server {{ _mgmt_pool | ipaddr('1') | ipaddr('address') }} use-vrf management

